Alphabet Inc. (GOOGL) — Q4 2024 Earnings Recap
Post-Earnings Analysis: January 29, 2025

HEADLINE RESULTS
Alphabet reported a strong Q4 2024, beating consensus on both revenue and earnings.
The stock rose 5.2% in after-hours trading.

FINANCIAL RESULTS vs. ESTIMATES
                    Actual      Estimate    Beat/Miss
Revenue:            $88.3B      $86.3B      +2.3% beat
Operating Income:   $28.9B      $26.8B      +7.8% beat
Net Income:         $25.1B      $23.4B      +7.3% beat
EPS:                $2.05       $1.92       +6.8% beat

SEGMENT BREAKDOWN
Google Search & Other:  $54.0B  (+14% YoY) — strongest growth in 6 quarters
YouTube Ads:            $10.5B  (+16% YoY) — Shorts monetization improving rapidly
Google Cloud:           $11.4B  (+29% YoY) — accelerating growth, now profitable
Google Other:           $10.8B  (+8% YoY)  — Pixel, subscriptions
Other Bets:             $1.6B   — Waymo losses narrowing to $1.1B

KEY TAKEAWAYS
1. Cloud Inflection: Google Cloud operating margin hit 10.8%, up from 5.2% in Q4 2023.
   Management highlighted 100+ $100M+ ARR customers, up from 70 a year ago. Gemini
   integration driving higher attach rates.

2. AI Monetization Progress: AI Overviews now generating higher revenue per query than
   traditional search in several verticals. Management noted "early but encouraging" trends.

3. Efficiency Gains: Total headcount declined 3% YoY while revenue grew 14%. Operating
   margin expanded 380bps to 32.7%.

4. 2025 Guidance: CapEx guided to $52-55B (vs. $50B consensus), reflecting aggressive
   AI infrastructure buildout. Revenue growth expected to remain "low teens" percent.

5. Capital Return: Board authorized $70B buyback (incremental). Q4 buybacks were $15.3B.

MANAGEMENT COMMENTARY HIGHLIGHTS
CEO Sundar Pichai: "Our AI-first strategy is delivering across every product surface.
Gemini is now deeply integrated into Search, Cloud, and Workspace."

CFO Ruth Porat: "We're seeing operating leverage improve as AI investments mature.
Our cloud business is now a consistent profitability contributor."

UPDATED THESIS
Results confirm GOOGL's position as a key AI beneficiary. Cloud acceleration and Search
resilience address the two biggest bear case concerns. Maintaining conviction.

ACTION: Maintain overweight position. Raise price target to $215 (from $200).
